WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.360
The adult wiring is lopsided.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.200
Was it built by cutting connections, or by strengthening them?

3
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.990
Pruning would start symmetric and delete the preferred-side connections.

4
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.810
Strengthening would keep both sides and grow the null side.

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.260
Remember, the null side is the side a null-direction stimulus comes from.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:27.703
Wei, Hamby, Zhou and Feller recorded pairs in mouse retina.

7
00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:31.823
Each pair was one starburst cell and one ganglion cell.

8
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:37.523
They stimulated one starburst cell at a time, and measured the inhibition the

9
00:00:37.523 --> 00:00:38.683
ganglion cell received.

10
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:44.187
At postnatal days 4 and 7, inhibition was similar from the two sides.

11
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:48.997
Predict. What should later recordings show under pruning?

12
00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:50.917
And what under strengthening?

13
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.557
Null-side inhibition grew.

14
00:00:59.497 --> 00:01:03.257
Preferred-side inhibition stayed about the same, and was still there in adult

15
00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:04.257
retina.

16
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.747
So development strengthened one side.

17
00:01:07.607 --> 00:01:08.727
It did not delete the other.

18
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.230
Later paired recordings from the same laboratory asked why.

19
00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.630
Null-side pairs had more synapses, not stronger ones.

20
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:26.573
One more test. Delete the starburst cells' vesicular GABA transporter.

21
00:01:27.573 --> 00:01:30.553
Their GABA release drops, but their acetylcholine stays.

22
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:36.793
Predict. If the veto were the whole mechanism, what would happen to direction

23
00:01:36.793 --> 00:01:37.793
selectivity?

24
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.737
Inhibition lost its direction tuning.

25
00:01:46.497 --> 00:01:50.257
But direction selectivity survived in a subset of ON-OFF cells.

26
00:01:51.317 --> 00:01:56.857
There, tuned excitation and the timing of residual inhibition supported selectivity.

27
00:01:57.957 --> 00:02:02.377
Direction tuning of inhibition is important, but some cells can remain selective

28
00:02:02.377 --> 00:02:03.377
without it.

29
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:11.710
Keep the sign. The strongest inhibition prefers roughly the direction the ganglion

30
00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.710
cell ignores.

31
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.333
It is best established in adult mouse and rabbit.

32
00:02:17.173 --> 00:02:20.613
The primate circuit is less studied, and the fly uses different cells.
